{
  "$schema": "Tool calls for CVE-2026-117569 (Kali-GPT through commit a608c74, CWE-78). NVD names execute_tool() in kali_gpt/tools/mcp_server.py and the scanner parameters `target`, `ports`, `domain`, `wordlist` and `url`, run through subprocess.run with shell=True; `tool` is the scanner the call selects. Each `payloads` entry carries one shell token in one of those parameters, with the argument, token and verdict ToolArgSinkGuard reports. Every value is an inert string: `id` is never run and nothing is scanned. `benign` holds calls the guard must run; `refused_although_well_formed` holds a legitimate URL the guard refuses because the server's shell would split it; `passes_by_design` holds values the guard's documented scope admits.",
